      "message": "fix(xtask): a FAIL before a stall stays a red main (review of #3489)\n\n- The report script treats a \"FAIL in\" progress line as a red main in\n  every case, also with no summary and a step timeout; the issue lists\n  those lines. \"Gate summary\" writes no timeout line after a FAIL.\n- No grep -q in a pipe under pipefail (SIGPIPE on a large summary read\n  as no FAIL row); a grep with no match no longer ends the summary step.\n- STALL comes from End::Stalled, not from a scan of the log text.\n- AGENTS.md \"Runner stops\": a second STALL of the same step at the same\n  commit is a red main. The decision file names the parent-pid kill gaps\n  (follow-up #3493).\n\nRefs #3303\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
